18 . Basically only three facts need to be established by the  claimants for assessing compensation in the case of death :
 (a) age of the deceased;
 (b) income of the deceased; and  (c) the number of dependents.

The issues to be determined by the Tribunal to arrive at the loss of  dependency are:
 (i) additions/deductions to be made for arriving at the income;
 (ii) the deduction to be made towards the personal living expenses  of the deceased; and  (iii) the multiplier to be applied with reference of the age of the  deceased.
